        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying an offset when you will not tend the fire</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Offsets need fuel and damper attention every 45 to 60 minutes. If you plan to set a temperature and walk away, a pellet or gravity-fed smoker will give you far better results with the time you have.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing total cooking area instead of the main grate</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Manufacturers add warming racks and fold-down shelves to the headline number. Compare the main grate's dimensions, and make sure a full brisket fits flat before you buy.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting the lid thermometer</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Built-in dome gauges often read well off the grate temperature. A dual-probe wireless thermometer at grate level and in the meat is the most useful thing you can add to any smoker.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Leaving ash and grease to build up</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Wet ash rusts steel and grease buildup can catch fire, and a clogged pellet fire pot can cause a burnback. Empty ash after each cook and follow the manual's cleaning schedule.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Storing pellets where they can get damp</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Moist pellets swell and jam the auger, one of the most common pellet grill failures. Keep pellets in a sealed bin indoors or in a dry garage.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

